<<<
special uses have -os; so dos (the musical note); bravados; calicos; crescendos; dittos; guanos; infernos; lumbagos. 4. When a vowel precedes the -o, -os is usual, perhaps because of the bizarre look of -ioes &e. 3 so arpeggios; baboos; bagnios; cameos; embryos; folios; punctilios. 5. The curtailed words made by dropping the second element of a
===
special uses have *-os*; so *dos* (the musical note); *bravados*; *calicos*; *crescendos*; *dittos*; *guanos*; *infernos*; *lumbagos*.

4. When a vowel precedes the *-o*, *-os* is usual, perhaps because of the bizarre look of *-ioes* &c.; so *arpeggios*; *baboos*; *bagnios*; *cameos*; *embryos*; *folios*; *punctilios*.

5. The curtailed words made by dropping the second element of a
